# C++20 Rules

- Prefer modern C++20 features when beneficial.
- Use concepts when they improve readability.
- Prefer std::span over raw pointer + size pairs.
- Prefer std::array over C arrays.
- Use std::optional for nullable return values.
- Use std::variant where appropriate.
- Prefer constexpr and consteval where useful.
- Use ranges carefully and only when readability improves.
- Avoid overengineering with templates.
- Avoid unnecessary metaprogramming.
- Prefer readable code over clever code.